# Nougat / structured extraction stub — arXiv:2308.05237

**Status:** stub. This replication did NOT run `nougat`, `marker`, or any other
Meta/structured-PDF extractor on the paper. The adjudication was done from the
`pdftotext` output at `work/paper.txt`, which was sufficient to cross-check
Sec. IV.A (dataset), Sec. IV.B (protocol), and Sec. IV.C + Table II (results).

## Why a stub is fine here
- Paper is 12 pages, plain 2-column IEEE-style layout, no complex equations that
  need MMD's LaTeX-preserving extraction.
- Table II (the reference for the headline claim) reads cleanly from `pdftotext`
  because it's a small text-only table.
- Downstream text-mining consumers of this replication dir can regenerate a real
  MMD by running: `nougat work/paper.pdf --out extraction/` (requires the nougat
  CLI + a GPU, ~2 min on uicgpu A100).

## Source references (from `work/paper.txt`)
- Sec. IV.A — Dataset: "200 records with 100 instances of fraudulent and
  non-fraudulent transactions" (paper's exact language, used to size our
  synthetic slice).
- Sec. IV.B — Protocol: "we utilized the Aer backend with the QasmSimulator ...
  implementing the COBYLA algorithm with a maximum iteration limit of 200".
- Sec. IV.C, Table II — Headline: QSVC + ZFeatureMap, F1 = 0.98 on both classes.
- Fig. 13 — VQC training-loss curves: ZFeatureMap converges to ~0.5, ZZ/Pauli
  plateau near ~0.95.

## To regenerate a real MMD extract
```
uv pip install nougat-ocr
nougat work/paper.pdf --out extraction/ --model 0.1.0-base
# → extraction/paper.mmd
mv extraction/paper.mmd extraction/nougat.mmd
```
